    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="26">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 26</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="26" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="100" ed="#liebermann"/>LXX. To fundes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="*" target="#Ine_26.lnote.oe.star"/> cildes fostre, ðy forman geare geselle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Ine_26.lnote.oe.21"/> VI<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Ine_26.lnote.oe.20-2"/> scill., ðy æfterran<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#Ine_26.lnote.oe.22"/> XII, ðy ðriddan XXX, siððan<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#Ine_26.lnote.oe.23"/> be his wlite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="26" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="100" ed="#liebermann"/>LXX. To fundenes cyldes fostre, ðy forman geare gesylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_26.lnote.oe.1"/> VI scll' ⁊ ðy æfteran geare XII ⁊ þy ðriddan XX ⁊ siððan be his wlite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="26" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="100" ed="#liebermann"/>Be fundenes cildes fostre. To fundenes cyldes fostre, ðu<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_26.lnote.oe.6"/> forman geare gesylle syx scill', ðu æftran twelf, ðu þriddan XXX, syððan be his wlite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="26" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="101" ed="#liebermann"/>Ad inuenticii<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Ine_26.lnote.oe.19"/> puerii uictum primo anno VI sol. reddantur, secundo anno XII solid., tercio anno XX sol., deinceps<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Ine_26.lnote.oe.20"/> secundum pretium suum.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="44" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be fundenes cildes fostre.] To fundenes<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#Ine_26.attnote.fn.4"/> cildes fostre, ðy forman geare geselle VI scill.,<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#Ine_26.attnote.fn.5"/> ðy æfterran XII<ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#Ine_26.attnote.fn.5-2"/>, ðy ðriddan XXX<ptr type="editorNote" n="6" target="#Ine_26.attnote.fn.6"/><ptr type="editorNote" n="5" target="#Ine_26.attnote.fn.5-3"/>, siððan be his wlite.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="26" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="392" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{LXX} To fundes cildes fostre: ðy forman geare geselle VI sciƚƚ, ðy æfterran XII, ðy ðriddan XXX, siððan be his wlite.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="101" ed="#liebermann"/>Zum Erziehungsgelde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_26.lnote.de.1"/> eines gefundenen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_26.lnote.de.2"/> Kindes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_26.lnote.de.3"/> gebe man<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_26.lnote.de.4"/> im ersten Jahre 6 Schill., im folgenden 12, im dritten 30<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_26.lnote.de.5"/>, späterhin nach seiner Körperbeschaffenheit.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_26.lnote.de.6"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">For the fostering of a foundling child let 6 shillings be given in the first year, 12 in the following, 30 in the third, and afterwards according to its appearance.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="45" ed="#attenborough"/>For the maintenance of a foundling 6 shillings shall be given in the first year, 12 shillings in the second, 30 shillings in the third, and afterwards [sums] according to his appearance<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_26.attnote.n.1"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="402" ed="#whitelock"/>For the maintenance of a foundling six shillings is to be paid<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_26.whinote.n.1"/> for the first year, 12 for the second, 30 for the third, and afterwards according to its appearance.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="393" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>For the fostering of a foundling: for the first year give 6 shillings; for the next, 12; for the third, 30; and afterwards according to his appearance.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_26.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">später geänd.</hi> ðy</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">later altered to ðy</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_26.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">101</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">inuentupium <hi rend="italic">K;</hi> inuentii <hi rend="italic">M Hk;</hi> inuenti <hi rend="italic">Co Br; vielleicht</hi> inuentiui <hi rend="italic">zu bessern</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">inuentupium K; inuentii M Hk; inuenti Co Br; perhaps to be corrected to inuentiui</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_26.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">101</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="spaced">postea</hi> <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">postea</hi> Lond</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_26.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_26.lnote.oe.star" n="*" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">bessere</hi> fundenes <hi rend="italic">aus H B Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">read fundenes from H B Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_26.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gesylle <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gesylle Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_26.lnote.oe.20-2" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">syx <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">syx Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_26.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">æftran geare twelf <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">æftran geare twelf Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_26.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">100</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">syþþan <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">syþþan Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_26.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Nicht bloss ‘Nahrung’; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Gl</hi> Erziehung 1—5; die 6 Schilling <hi rend="italic">ebd.</hi> 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Not merely ‘food’; <hi rend="italic">cf. Gl</hi> Erziehung 1—5; the 6 shillings <hi rend="italic">ibid.</hi> 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_26.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Findling; Bastard 4. Q scheint ein Wort selbst zu bilden</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Findling; Bastard 4. Q seems to coin a word of his own</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_26.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Sussex war zwar erst damals bekehrt; doch denkt Ine nicht vorwiegend an heidnische Eltern. Eher an nicht anerkannte Uneheliche (zu deren Aussetzung <hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> Wilda 726; Ducange s. v. <hi rend="italic">collectus, sanguinolentus</hi>), von denen c. 27 handelt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Sussex, it is true, was only converted at that time; but Ine is not thinking primarily of heathen parents. Rather of unacknowledged illegitimate children (on their exposure <hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> Wilda 726; Ducange s. v. <hi rend="italic">collectus, sanguinolentus</hi>), with whom c. 27 deals</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_26.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Die Staatsbehörde, da der König Wergeld für Tötung des Findlings bezieht; der Staat will die Ausgesetzten retten; Maurer <hi rend="italic">Wasserweihe</hi> 226. Der persönliche Herr war unerkennbar; ein Grundherr existierte nicht überall und konnte schwerlich vom Staate so belastet werden</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The state authority, since the king receives the wergild for the killing of the foundling; the state wishes to save exposed children; Maurer <hi rend="italic">Wasserweihe</hi> 226. The personal lord could not be identified; a landlord did not exist everywhere and could hardly be burdened in this way by the state</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_26.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">H und Q: 20</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">H and Q: 20</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_26.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘appearance’ Toller, ‘Gestaltnis der Person’ Schmid; <hi rend="italic">pretium</hi> nimmt Q aus VI As 6, 1; 3, hier unpassend</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">‘appearance’ Toller, ‘form of the person’ Schmid; Q takes <hi rend="italic">pretium</hi> from VI As 6, 1; 3, unsuitably here</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_26.attnote.fn.4" n="4" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope></bibl><label>fundenes</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">fundes</hi>. E. <hi rend="italic">fundenes</hi>. H &amp; B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_26.attnote.fn.5" n="5" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope></bibl><label>xxx</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">⁊. H.</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">The number 5 is printed 3 times on the page (26, 26, 26), with one footnote.</note></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_26.attnote.fn.5-2" n="5" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope></bibl><label>xxx</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">⁊. H.</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">The number 5 is printed 3 times on the page (26, 26, 26), with one footnote.</note></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_26.attnote.fn.5-3" n="5" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope></bibl><label>xxx</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">⁊. H.</seg><note type="remark" resp="#claude">The number 5 is printed 3 times on the page (26, 26, 26), with one footnote.</note></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_26.attnote.fn.6" n="6" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">44</biblScope></bibl><label>xxx</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">xx</hi>. H &amp; Quad.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_26.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">186</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">It is not clear to me what is meant—whether a strong healthy child needs more sustenance, or whether more should be paid for a child which appears to be of aristocratic origin. Schmid translates ‘Gestaltnis der Person’; Liebermann, ‘Körperbeschaffenheit.’</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Ine_26.whinote.n.1" n="1" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">402</biblScope></bibl><label>paid</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Probably by the king’s representative, for it was the king who would be entitled to the wergild of a person of unknown kin.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
  </text>
